["e","2·32","What is an expert system?","A computer program that imitates the decision-making ability of a human expert in a specific field",["A program that can do any task a human can","A website that lists experts","A robot that teaches itself"],"It copies an expert.","That is the definition of an expert system."],
["e","2·32","An expert system is focused on…","one field",["every field at once","no particular field","only mathematics"],"A specific field.","It solves problems only in its own area."],
["e","2·32","In an expert system, the expert’s knowledge is written as…","IF-THEN rules",["neural layers","membership curves","tokens"],"It uses rules.","Expert systems use IF-THEN rules."],
["e","2·32","Why is an expert system “always available”?","It gives consistent advice at any time, even when the human expert is not around",["It never needs electricity","It can be used by only one person","It learns by itself at night"],"No waiting for the expert.","It gives consistent advice at any time."],
["e","2·33","What are the three main components of an expert system?","User interface, inference engine, and knowledge base",["Sensors, actuators, and performance measure","Input, hidden, and output layers","Tokenizer, parser, and corpus"],"Ask, infer, store.","User ⇄ User Interface ⇄ Inference Engine ⇄ Knowledge Base."],
["e","2·33","Which component stores facts and rules gathered from human experts?","Knowledge base",["Inference engine","User interface","Working memory"],"The storage.","The knowledge base."],
["e","2·33","Which component applies rules to the knowledge base to reach conclusions?","Inference engine",["Knowledge base","User interface","Explanation facility"],"It infers.","The inference engine."],
["e","2·33","Which component lets the user ask questions and receive answers?","User interface",["Knowledge base","Inference engine","Working memory"],"What the user sees.","The user interface."],
["e","2·33","Who supplies the knowledge for an expert system?","The domain expert",["The knowledge engineer","The user","The inference engine"],"A doctor or technician.","The domain expert supplies the knowledge."],
["e","2·33","Who puts the expert’s knowledge into the system?","The knowledge engineer",["The domain expert","The user","The explanation facility"],"The builder.","The knowledge engineer."],
["e","2·34","Which part stores the facts of the current problem, such as the user’s answers?","Working memory",["Knowledge base","Inference engine","Explanation facility"],"It remembers the current problem.","Working memory."],
["e","2·34","Which part explains how the system reached its conclusion, so the user can trust it?","Explanation facility",["Working memory","Knowledge acquisition","User interface"],"It answers “why?”.","Explanation facility."],
["e","2·34","Which part helps add or update the knowledge in the knowledge base?","Knowledge acquisition",["Working memory","Explanation facility","Inference engine"],"Getting knowledge in.","Knowledge acquisition."],
["e","2·34","“The charger may be faulty BECAUSE the computer has no power light AND the charger is plugged in (Rule 1).” is an example of the…","Explanation facility",["Working memory","Knowledge base","User interface"],"It says why.","That is an explanation of the conclusion."],
["e","2·35","Which of these is a FACT in the knowledge base?","The laptop does not turn on.",["IF the computer has no power light AND the charger is plugged in THEN the charger may be faulty","IF the computer has a power light BUT the screen is black THEN the monitor may be faulty","Rule 1"],"A statement known to be true.","Facts are statements known to be true; rules are IF-THEN statements."],
["e","2·35","Rule 2: IF the computer has a power light BUT the screen is black THEN…","the monitor or the display cable may be faulty",["the charger or the power supply may be faulty","the battery is empty","the keyboard is faulty"],"The screen is the problem.","Rule 2 points to the monitor or the display cable."],
["e","2·35","Rule 1: IF the computer has no power light AND the charger is plugged in THEN…","the charger or the power supply may be faulty",["the monitor or the display cable may be faulty","the screen is black","the keyboard is faulty"],"No power light.","Rule 1 points to the charger or the power supply."],
["e","2·36","The inference engine decides…","which rules to apply, and in what order",["which facts are true","who the domain expert is","what the user types"],"It chooses the rules.","It decides which rules to apply, and in what order."],
["e","2·36","Forward chaining starts from…","the facts",["a possible conclusion","the THEN part of the rules","the user interface"],"The symptoms.","Forward chaining starts from the facts."],
["e","2·36","Backward chaining starts from…","a possible conclusion and checks if the facts support it",["the facts and applies every rule","the user interface","the knowledge acquisition facility"],"Testing a guess.","Backward chaining starts from a possible conclusion."],
["e","2·36","“Here are the symptoms. What is the problem?” is which kind of chaining?","Forward chaining",["Backward chaining","Cross chaining","Random chaining"],"From facts to conclusion.","Forward chaining."],
["e","2·36","“Is the problem the charger? Are the facts true?” is which kind of chaining?","Backward chaining",["Forward chaining","Cross chaining","Random chaining"],"From a guess to the facts.","Backward chaining."],
["e","2·39","Which kind of reasoning is data-driven?","Forward chaining",["Backward chaining","Both of them","Neither of them"],"Data = the facts.","Forward chaining is data-driven; backward chaining is goal-driven."],
["e","2·37","When does a rule fire?","Only when all of its IF conditions are true",["When at least one IF condition is true","When the user presses a button","When the THEN part is true"],"All of them.","A rule fires only when all of its IF conditions are true."],
["e","2·37","The facts are “no power light” and “the charger is plugged in”. Which rule fires?","Rule 1 only",["Rule 2 only","Both rules","Neither rule"],"Check each IF part.","Rule 1 fires. Rule 2 needs a power light."],
["e","2·37","Why does Rule 2 not fire when the computer has no power light?","Its condition “has a power light” is false",["Because it is written after Rule 1","Because the charger is plugged in","Because it has no THEN part"],"Check the IF part.","A rule fires only when all IF conditions are true."],
["e","2·38","What is the first step to create an expert system?","Define: choose a problem and a narrow field",["Test the system","Build the interface","Write the rules"],"Start with the problem.","Steps: Define, Gather, Write Rules, Build, Test."],
["e","2·38","What is the correct order of the steps to create an expert system?","Define → Gather → Write Rules → Build → Test",["Gather → Define → Build → Write Rules → Test","Build → Define → Gather → Test → Write Rules","Write Rules → Define → Gather → Test → Build"],"Test comes last.","Define, Gather, Write Rules, Build, Test."],
["e","2·38","What do we do in the last step of creating an expert system?","Test real cases, then fix and improve the rules",["Choose a narrow field","Collect knowledge from experts","Turn knowledge into rules"],"Last step.","Test: try real cases, then fix and improve the rules."],
["e","2·38","Which tool will we use in the laboratory to build a simple expert system?","Google Forms",["Microsoft Excel","Python Turtle","Photoshop"],"A Google tool.","Our laboratory uses Google Forms."],
["e","2·39","A system that makes decisions using IF-THEN rules is a…","Rule-based system",["Neural network","Crisp value","Corpus"],"Rules.","Rule-based system."],
["e","2·39","A ready-made tool with an inference engine and interface, where you only add the knowledge, is an…","Expert system shell",["Knowledge engineer","Explanation facility","Inference rule"],"An empty shell.","Expert system shell."],
["e","2·39","A rule of thumb based on experience that helps find a good answer quickly is a…","Heuristic",["Corpus","Token","Shell"],"A shortcut.","Heuristic."],
["e","2·40","MYCIN was developed at which university in the 1970s?","Stanford University",["Harvard University","Dartmouth College","Carnegie Mellon University"],"A university in California.","MYCIN was developed at Stanford University in the 1970s."],
["e","2·40","What was the purpose of MYCIN?","Help doctors identify bacteria that cause serious infections and suggest treatment",["Translate languages","Play chess","Control a robot vacuum"],"Medical.","It helped doctors identify bacteria and suggest treatment."],
["e","2·40","How did MYCIN work?","It asked the doctor a series of questions and applied hundreds of IF-THEN rules",["It learned from millions of photos","It translated the doctor’s speech","It used only one rule"],"Questions and rules.","It asked questions and applied hundreds of IF-THEN rules."],
["e","2·40","What was the result of MYCIN’s tests?","Its advice was comparable to human specialists, but it was never used in real patient care",["It replaced all doctors","It always gave wrong advice","It was used in every hospital"],"Good, but never used.","Comparable advice, but never used in real patient care."],
["e","2·40","What is the lesson of MYCIN?","Expert systems can work well in a narrow field, but responsibility for decisions stays with people",["Expert systems should replace doctors","Expert systems work well in every field","Expert systems never make mistakes"],"Who stays responsible?","Responsibility for decisions stays with people."],
["e","2·41","Which is an advantage of expert systems?","Consistent answers every time",["They learn on their own","They have common sense","They work in many fields"],"Always the same answer.","Other advantages: available any time, keeps the knowledge of experts, faster than a manual, cheaper than many experts."],
["e","2·41","Which is a limitation of expert systems?","They cannot learn on their own; rules must be updated by people",["They are available any time","They are faster than looking up a manual","They keep the knowledge of experts even if they leave"],"The others are advantages.","Limitations: narrow field, cannot learn, no common sense, slow to collect knowledge, wrong rules give wrong advice."],
["e","2·42","In the umbrella expert system, “IF it is raining THEN bring an umbrella” belongs to the…","Knowledge base (a rule)",["Inference engine","User interface","Working memory"],"It is an IF-THEN rule.","Rules are stored in the knowledge base; the inference engine applies them."],
["e","2·43","According to the conclusion slide, who stays responsible for decisions when fuzzy systems, chatbots, and expert systems help us decide?","People",["The fuzzy system","The chatbot","The expert system"],"AI needs human judgment.","AI needs human judgment: people stay responsible."]
