["r","Knowledge Base","Inference Engine","The knowledge base stores facts and rules. The inference engine applies them."],
["r","Input Layer","Output Layer","Input receives the data. Output gives the result. Hidden layers are in between."],
["s","Uninformed (Blind) Search","Informed (Heuristic) Search","Uninformed has no extra information (BFS, DFS). Informed uses a heuristic (A*)."],
["s","Breadth-First Search (BFS)","Depth-First Search (DFS)","BFS: shallowest first, queue (FIFO). DFS: deepest first, stack (LIFO)."],
["s","Queue","Stack","Queue = First In, First Out (BFS). Stack = Last In, First Out (DFS)."],
["s","Transition Model","Goal Test","The transition model gives the result of an action. The goal test asks if this is the goal."],
["s","Branching Factor (b)","Depth (d)","Branching factor = children per node. Depth = steps from the root."],
["s","Frontier","Leaf","The frontier holds nodes waiting to be expanded. A leaf has no children."],
["f","Crisp Logic","Fuzzy Logic","Crisp: only 0 or 1, sharp cut-off. Fuzzy: any value from 0 to 1, gradual change."],
["f","Linguistic Variable","Linguistic Terms","The variable is Temperature. The terms are Cold, Warm, and Hot."],
["f","Fuzzification","Defuzzification","Fuzzification: crisp input becomes membership degrees (first step). Defuzzification: fuzzy output becomes one crisp number (last step)."],
["f","Aggregation","Defuzzification","Aggregation combines the rule results into one fuzzy output. Defuzzification turns it into a crisp value."],
["f","Rule Evaluation","Aggregation","Rule evaluation applies each IF-THEN rule. Aggregation combines all the results."],
["f","Triangular","Trapezoidal","Triangular peaks at one point. Trapezoidal has a flat top (1 over a range)."],
["f","Trapezoidal","Gaussian","Trapezoidal has straight sides and a flat top. Gaussian is a smooth bell curve."],
["f","Fuzzy AND","Fuzzy OR","AND takes the minimum (smaller). OR takes the maximum (bigger)."],
["f","Centroid","Weighted Average","Centroid is the center of gravity (most common). Weighted average is the method used in the lecture examples."],
["f","Rule Base","Universe of Discourse","The rule base is all the IF-THEN rules. The universe of discourse is the range of values (10°C to 40°C)."],
["n","Natural Language Understanding (NLU)","Natural Language Generation (NLG)","NLU figures out meaning and intent. NLG produces the computer's own sentences."],
["n","Stemming","Lemmatization","Stemming cuts to the root (playing → play). Lemmatization gives the dictionary form (better → good)."],
["n","Intent","Entity","Intent is what the user wants to do (turn on). An entity is a detail (lights, kitchen)."],
["n","Token","Tokenization","A token is a piece of text. Tokenization is splitting the text into tokens."],
["n","Stop Words","Entities","Stop words (the, is) carry little meaning. Entities (place, time, object) carry key details."],
["n","Syntactic Level","Semantic Level","Syntactic = grammar and structure. Semantic = meaning of words and sentences."],
["n","Semantic Level","Pragmatic Level","Semantic = what the words mean. Pragmatic = what the speaker really means in context."],
["n","Lexical Level","Syntactic Level","Lexical = words and their forms. Syntactic = how words are arranged in a sentence."],
["n","Part-of-Speech (POS) Tagging","Named Entity Recognition (NER)","POS tagging labels the type of every word. NER finds names of people, places, dates, and organizations."],
["n","Rule-based Chatbot","AI-based Chatbot","Rule-based follows fixed rules and keywords. AI-based uses machine learning."],
["n","Sentiment","Sentiment Analysis","Sentiment is the feeling of a text. Sentiment analysis is the task of finding it."],
["e","Knowledge Base","Working Memory","The knowledge base stores the expert's facts and rules. Working memory stores the facts of the current problem."],
["e","Domain Expert","Knowledge Engineer","The domain expert supplies the knowledge. The knowledge engineer puts it into the system."],
["e","Facts","Rules","Facts are statements known to be true. Rules are IF-THEN statements."],
["e","Forward Chaining","Backward Chaining","Forward: facts → conclusion (data-driven). Backward: possible conclusion → facts (goal-driven)."],
["e","Explanation Facility","Knowledge Acquisition","Explanation facility explains the conclusion. Knowledge acquisition adds or updates knowledge."],
["e","Inference Engine","User Interface","The inference engine applies the rules. The user interface lets the user ask and receive answers."],
["e","Expert System","Expert System Shell","An expert system is the finished program. A shell is a ready-made tool where you only add the knowledge."],
["e","Knowledge Acquisition (process)","Knowledge Engineer","Knowledge acquisition is the process of gathering knowledge. The knowledge engineer is the person who does it."]
